        <mxCell id="EyT6oF-ovBxys-f1xOxE-25" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;OPTIMISED GROUND SEGMENT FRAMEWORK FOR EFFICIENT PROCESSING OF&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;COPERNICUS SENTINEL-2 DATA STREAMS&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The proposed framework enables real-time satellite telemetry ingestion through FPGA-accelerated decoding combined with a distributed microservice pipeline. By offloading frame validation to hardware and leveraging a message-driven processing architecture, the system significantly reduces end-to-end latency while supporting elastic scaling across processing nodes. The design ensures high data freshness, fault isolation, and seamless integration with large-scale analytics and AI platforms, forming a robust foundation for next-generation Earth observation missions.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="470" x="100" y="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zbvoaHkvpSs7XJc97ERu-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Satellite Transmitter&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ol data-start=&quot;280&quot; data-end=&quot;498&quot;&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;280&quot; data-end=&quot;318&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;283&quot; data-end=&quot;318&quot;&gt;Creates a fake image (checkerboard)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;319&quot; data-end=&quot;370&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;322&quot; data-end=&quot;370&quot;&gt;Converts image pixels into compact binary format&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;371&quot; data-end=&quot;402&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;374&quot; data-end=&quot;402&quot;&gt;Splits the data into packets&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;403&quot; data-end=&quot;430&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;406&quot; data-end=&quot;430&quot;&gt;Adds a header (metadata)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;431&quot; data-end=&quot;455&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;434&quot; data-end=&quot;455&quot;&gt;Simulates packet loss&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;431&quot; data-end=&quot;455&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;434&quot; data-end=&quot;455&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Writes the transmitted stream to a file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;500&quot; data-end=&quot;585&quot;&gt;That file (&lt;code data-start=&quot;511&quot; data-end=&quot;527&quot;&gt;raw_stream.bin&lt;/code&gt;) represents what a real satellite would transmit over RF.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;500&quot; data-end=&quot;585&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;828&quot; data-end=&quot;938&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Image size = 256 × 256 pixels&lt;br data-start=&quot;859&quot; data-end=&quot;862&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Each packet carries max 512 bytes&lt;br data-start=&quot;897&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;• 5% of packets are randomly dropped&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;500&quot; data-end=&quot;585&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;940&quot; data-end=&quot;961&quot;&gt;So you’re simulating:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-start=&quot;962&quot; data-end=&quot;1021&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;a camera&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;limited packet size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;noisy space transmission&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="470" width="470" x="-350" y="-320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLQxsfm0ZKUBVexxL3yo-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Ingest Service&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ol data-start=&quot;280&quot; data-end=&quot;498&quot;&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;280&quot; data-end=&quot;318&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;283&quot; data-end=&quot;318&quot;&gt;Creates a fake image (checkerboard)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;319&quot; data-end=&quot;370&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;322&quot; data-end=&quot;370&quot;&gt;Converts image pixels into compact binary format&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;371&quot; data-end=&quot;402&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;374&quot; data-end=&quot;402&quot;&gt;Splits the data into packets&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;403&quot; data-end=&quot;430&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;406&quot; data-end=&quot;430&quot;&gt;Adds a header (metadata)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;431&quot; data-end=&quot;455&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;434&quot; data-end=&quot;455&quot;&gt;Simulates packet loss&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;431&quot; data-end=&quot;455&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;434&quot; data-end=&quot;455&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Writes the transmitted stream to a file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;500&quot; data-end=&quot;585&quot;&gt;That file (&lt;code data-start=&quot;511&quot; data-end=&quot;527&quot;&gt;raw_stream.bin&lt;/code&gt;) represents what a real satellite would transmit over RF.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;500&quot; data-end=&quot;585&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;828&quot; data-end=&quot;938&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Image size = 256 × 256 pixels&lt;br data-start=&quot;859&quot; data-end=&quot;862&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Each packet carries max 512 bytes&lt;br data-start=&quot;897&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;• 5% of packets are randomly dropped&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;500&quot; data-end=&quot;585&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;940&quot; data-end=&quot;961&quot;&gt;So you’re simulating:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-start=&quot;962&quot; data-end=&quot;1021&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;a camera&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;limited packet size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;noisy space transmission&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="470" width="470" x="180" y="-330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
